    "scope": "Complete connected Kuzminsky House exterior at Yasnaya Polyana: mapped compact white two-storey block, green standing-seam hip roof and two pale capped chimney stacks. Central shallow risalits and triangular pediments, tall arched upper glazing, supported front balcony with open lattice proxies and brackets, recessed lower front/rear entrances with closed treads/masonry stair sides, and northeast side porch with a low green roof, posts, recessed door and treads. Short approximate rear threshold treads follow the coarse original grade. Long rear elevation and blind side panels follow ordinary pictures with approximate hidden bay inventory. No copied texts, plaques, furnishings, artworks or photograph pixels.",
    "identityBasis": "Named Флигель Кузминских POI and way167382261 identify this house independently from Tolstoy and Volkonsky houses. The mapped long southeast edge fixes+X southwest along the facade and+Z southeast into the front garden; axes baked east/up/south, heading0. Ordinary southeast and northeast photographs confirm the compact five-bay long fronts, central arched upper opening/pediment and northeast side porch. Photo-visible balcony, treads and side porch extend outside the simple map rectangle.",
    "heightBasis": "Approximate photo-led medium-fi scale: mapped17.95m by11.7m envelope, lower storey3m and upper storey3.8m, hip roof1.5m rise above6.8m eaves and two chimney caps about9.6m above floor. Map nominal8m is a scale cue, not a survey. Front/rear central panels, historic levels, thresholds, hidden bays and porch dimensions remain approximate.",
    "terrainBasis": "Retained standard Protomaps20261020 and Mapzen ground; outside front garden provider[0,7] supplies227.14409009244258m datum. Main boundary grades-0.048..0.944m, floor+1.2m and closed foundation-0.3m. Original garden/approaches, estate neighbors, roads and ponds remain. Coarse exposed plinth, historical thresholds and accessibility approximate; no bespoke terrain or flattening."
